    "steps": [
      "Boil the spaghetti in a pot of well-salted water, following the packet time, until al dente.",
      "Scoop out a cup of the pasta water and set it aside, then drain the spaghetti in a colander.",
      "Warm the olive oil and butter together in a skillet over medium heat until the butter has melted.",
      "Stir in the garlic, then crack the eggs into the skillet. Fry until the whites are firm; the yolks stay runny, so cook longer if you like them set.",
      "Add the drained spaghetti, parsley and capers to the skillet. Toss well, breaking the yolks, until every strand is coated.",
      "Loosen with a splash of the saved pasta water only if the pasta looks dry, stirring until the coating is loose and creamy.",
      "Tip onto a plate, scatter the Pecorino Romano over the top and finish with the crisp pangrattato breadcrumbs.",
      "You nailed it! Grab a plate and dig in."
